  "section_notes": "S2 has no permanent sales bar: exceeding 5% triggers only review and a corrective-action plan, so a model such as the Hearth 10 (6.2%) can remain on sale, and the transition is open-ended (999). S5 makes recall discretionary with the 8/100k threshold serving only as a notification trigger, so the Ember 8 (9.9/100k) faces no mandatory recall, and S4's 'no sooner than 36 months' sets a floor with no stated deadline. S3's 72-month retrofit window sits exactly at the Northwind red line, and S1 reporting is strict on both scope and timing."
